      "hub_id": null,
      "version": "1.1.0",
      "description": "<h2>Updates/Fixes:</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Added to SBIH quest</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Added ability for other locales (ships with en &amp; ru, defaults to en for all others but you can add custom locales in the same format as the other json files!)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Added some items to traders (only main gun and ammo - still need trader data)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Fixed formatting for Linux users (should be at least - let me know if not)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Added mastery and presets</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Accurate handbook data</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Installation</h2>\n<p><strong>Please make sure to delete the old mod folder /SPT/user/mods/MC-MXLR/ before transferring the new folder over! Some files got renamed so it would be better to replace the whole folder just in case.</strong></p>\n<h2>Other</h2>\n<p>I am not sure if this will fix the issue regarding ODT’s Item Info; I apologize I ran out of time to try and tackle that issue, but hope to do so this week if this update does not fix it. Also I got a report that a testing profile was detecting stray items leftover from the old version of the mod, but I was not able to recreate that. Please report any issues you see in the comments.</p>\n<p>Special thanks to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Kibb on Discord for the Linux fix &amp; testing</li>\n<li>aklyashkin on Discord for the ru translation</li>\n</ul>\n",
